CALSCALE:GREGORIAN
METHOD:PUBLISH
X-WR-CALNAME:Going Above\, Gulf Coast Home Maintenance
X-WR-CALDESC:For the homeowner who wants to stay ahead of everything. Gener
 al maintenance guidance\, not a substitute for a licensed inspector\, cont
 ractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
X-WR-TIMEZONE:America/Chicago
REFRESH-INTERVAL;VALUE=DURATION:P1D
X-PUBLISHED-TTL:P1D
COLOR:olivedrab
X-APPLE-CALENDAR-COLOR:#5D6B3A
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-jan-attic-check@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260102
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:1
SUMMARY:Check the attic after winter rain
DESCRIPTION:Look for daylight through the roof deck\, damp or matted insula
 tion\, and water stains on the framing.\n\nWhy: a small roof leak shows up
  in the attic long before it shows up on your ceiling. Winter rain is the 
 easiest time to catch one.\n\nHow to: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com
 /guides/#jan-attic-check\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a substitut
 e for a licensed inspector\, contractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-feb-caulk@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260202
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:1
SUMMARY:Walk the exterior and re-caulk
DESCRIPTION:Re-caulk gaps around windows\, doors\, and any penetration thro
 ugh the wall.\n\nWhy: caulk is the cheapest material on the house and the 
 first line against wind-driven rain. On the coast it fails in 2–4 years.
 \n\nHow to: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#feb-caulk\n\nGene
 ral maintenance guidance\, not a substitute for a licensed inspector\, con
 tractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-mar-grading@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260301
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260302
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:1
SUMMARY:Check the grading around the house
DESCRIPTION:Walk the perimeter after a hard rain. Look for settling\, crack
 s\, and standing water.\n\nWhy: the ground should fall away from the house
 . Gulf Coast soils shift\, and grading that worked at closing may not work
  three years later.\n\nHow to: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides
 /#mar-grading\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a substitute for a lic
 ensed inspector\, contractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-apr-spigots-irrigation@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260401
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260402
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:1
SUMMARY:Check spigots and service irrigation
DESCRIPTION:Check hose bibs and outdoor spigots for leaks. Service the irri
 gation system if you have one.\n\nWhy: a spigot that weeps against the fou
 ndation all summer does quiet\, steady damage\, and shows up on the water 
 bill.\n\nHow to: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#apr-spigots-
 irrigation\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a substitute for a licens
 ed inspector\, contractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-may-secure-exterior@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260501
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260502
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:1
SUMMARY:Inspect roof edges\, secure loose items
DESCRIPTION:Inspect soffit vents and roof edges. Secure sheds\, fencing\, a
 nd anything that becomes a projectile.\n\nWhy: most wind damage starts at 
 an edge. Once wind gets under the roof edge or through an open soffit\, it
  works on the whole roof.\n\nHow to: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/
 guides/#may-secure-exterior\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a substi
 tute for a licensed inspector\, contractor\, or your insurance policy term
 s.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-jun-attic-ventilation@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260601
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260602
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:1
SUMMARY:Check attic ventilation and insulation
DESCRIPTION:Check that soffit and ridge vents are clear\, and measure insul
 ation depth.\n\nWhy: a poorly vented attic bakes the roof deck from undern
 eath and shortens shingle life\, on top of what it costs you in cooling.\n
 \nHow to: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#jun-attic-ventilati
 on\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a substitute for a licensed inspe
 ctor\, contractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-jul-humidity@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260701
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260702
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:1
SUMMARY:Check indoor humidity
DESCRIPTION:Measure indoor relative humidity. Aim for 45–55%. Run a dehum
 idifier if you are above that.\n\nWhy: above 60% indoors you are growing m
 old and inviting dust mites\, whatever the thermostat says.\n\nHow to: htt
 ps://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#jul-humidity\n\nGeneral maintena
 nce guidance\, not a substitute for a licensed inspector\, contractor\, or
  your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-aug-photograph-valuables@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260801
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260802
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:1
SUMMARY:Photograph big-ticket items
DESCRIPTION:Photograph big-ticket items and store the photos somewhere off-
 site or in the cloud.\n\nWhy: proof of ownership is what turns a claim int
 o a payment\, and it is worthless if it only exists on a phone that went w
 ith the house.\n\nHow to: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#aug
 -photograph-valuables\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a substitute f
 or a licensed inspector\, contractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-sep-sump-drainage@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:1
SUMMARY:Test the sump pump\, clear drainage
DESCRIPTION:Test the sump pump if you have one. Clear drainage swales and d
 itches.\n\nWhy: a sump pump that has not run in months is a sump pump you 
 should not assume works. Blocked ditches move the water to your yard.\n\nH
 ow to: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#sep-sump-drainage\n\nG
 eneral maintenance guidance\, not a substitute for a licensed inspector\, 
 contractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-oct-chimney@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:1
SUMMARY:Service the fireplace or chimney
DESCRIPTION:Service the fireplace or chimney before first use.\n\nWhy: an u
 nused flue collects nests\, debris\, and moisture damage over a long warm 
 season.\n\nHow to: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#oct-chimne
 y\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a substitute for a licensed inspec
 tor\, contractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-nov-gutters-fascia@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:1
SUMMARY:Clear gutters\, check fascia and trim
DESCRIPTION:Clear the gutters after leaf drop. Check the fascia and trim fo
 r rot.\n\nWhy: fascia is where a gutter that overflowed all year finally s
 hows the damage\, and rotten fascia is how the gutter comes off in the nex
 t storm.\n\nHow to: https://gulfcoasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#nov-gutte
 rs-fascia\n\nGeneral maintenance guidance\, not a substitute for a license
 d inspector\, contractor\, or your insurance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-dec-watch-list@gulfcoast-home-maintenance
DTSTAMP:20260813T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
SEQUENCE:1
SUMMARY:Update the Big Ticket Watch List
DESCRIPTION:Update your Big Ticket Watch List with anything you replaced or
  serviced this year.\n\nWhy: the list is what turns a surprise roof into a
  planned roof. One update a year keeps it honest.\n\nHow to: https://gulfc
 oasthomemaintenance.com/guides/#dec-watch-list\n\nGeneral maintenance guid
 ance\, not a substitute for a licensed inspector\, contractor\, or your in
 surance policy terms.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Home Maintenance
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
